      "patient_response": "Worrying? I mean, not really. I don't sit around stressing about things that haven't happened. I actually try not to think too far ahead because then I just get overwhelmed. Like last week, I was trying to figure out if I should finally fix my car—it's this 2008 Honda Civic, and the AC has been busted for like three years. Summer is brutal. You roll the windows down, but then you can't hear the radio. And I need the radio because I listen to this one morning show where they do these prank calls. They had this one guy call a pizza place and try to order a tire. The guy at the pizza place was getting so mad, it was hilarious. I actually used to deliver pizzas for a few months right after high school. Worst job ever. The smell of pepperoni just gets stuck in your car's upholstery, you know? I tried everything to get it out—baking soda, those little pine tree air fresheners. I bought like five of the \"Black Ice\" ones and hung them all on the rearview mirror. \n\nWait, what were we talking about? Oh, worrying. Yeah, no, I don't really worry about stuff unless it's like, right in front of my face.",
